> > so using channel="stable" could cause this failure, but only for mir-opt tests with --bless (x test mir-opt --bless) mode. But reading the issue title you get the same error with x build too I guess?
> 
> The error is given out when the compiler is built internally during bootstrapping rust compiler by following command: `python3 src/bootstrap/bootstrap.py test --target x86_64-poky-linux-gnu `
> 
> If `x build` command is given explicitly in terminal, it works fine.

Can you apply the following patch and try testing it again? It should fix the problem you are facing.

```diff
diff --git a/src/bootstrap/src/core/build_steps/test.rs b/src/bootstrap/src/core/build_steps/test.rs
index 92140b00da8..a9ec804e65d 100644
--- a/src/bootstrap/src/core/build_steps/test.rs
+++ b/src/bootstrap/src/core/build_steps/test.rs
@@ -1527,11 +1527,15 @@ fn run(self, builder: &Builder<'_>) {
             for target in targets {
                 run(target);
 
-                let panic_abort_target = builder.ensure(MirOptPanicAbortSyntheticTarget {
-                    compiler: self.compiler,
-                    base: target,
-                });
-                run(panic_abort_target);
+                if builder.config.channel == "dev" || builder.config.channel == "nightly" {
+                    let panic_abort_target = builder.ensure(MirOptPanicAbortSyntheticTarget {
+                        compiler: self.compiler,
+                        base: target,
+                    });
+                    run(panic_abort_target);
+                } else {
+                    builder.info(&format!("INFO: The panic=abort MIR-opt test was skipped because it cannot run on the {} channel, as it requires nightly features.\n", builder.config.channel));
+                }
             }
         } else {
             run(self.target);
